{"bargaining_script": "ਇਹ ਕਿੰਨੇ ਦਾ ਹੈ? (how much?) → ਬਹੁਤ ਮਹਿੰਗਾ ਹੈ! (too pricey!) → ਥੋੜ੍ਹਾ ਸਸਤਾ ਕਰੋ (make it cheaper) → ਛੋਟ ਦਿਓ (give a discount) → ਚੰਗਾ, ਪੈਕ ਕਰ ਦਿਓ! (done, pack it!)", "classifiers": [{"en": "ਇੱਕ ਕਿਤਾਬ", "hi": "एक किताब", "note": "one book — number + noun, no extras", "r": "ikk kitāb"}, {"en": "ਦੋ ਕਿਤਾਬਾਂ", "hi": "दो किताबें", "note": "two books — the noun itself goes plural (-ਾਂ)", "r": "do kitābān"}, {"en": "ਤਿੰਨ ਰੁਪਏ", "hi": "तीन रुपये", "note": "three rupees — same pattern as Hindi", "r": "tinn rupae"}], "colors": [{"en": "red", "hi": "लाल", "note": "ਲਾਲ never changes for gender", "r": "lāl", "t": "ਲਾਲ"}, {"en": "blue", "hi": "नीला", "note": "ਨੀਲੀ with feminine nouns", "r": "nīlā", "t": "ਨੀਲਾ"}, {"en": "green", "hi": "हरा", "note": "ਹਰੀ with feminine nouns", "r": "harā", "t": "ਹਰਾ"}, {"en": "yellow", "hi": "पीला", "note": "ਪੀਲੀ with feminine nouns", "r": "pīlā", "t": "ਪੀਲਾ"}, {"en": "black", "hi": "काला", "note": "ਕਾਲੀ with feminine nouns", "r": "kālā", "t": "ਕਾਲਾ"}, {"en": "white", "hi": "सफ़ेद", "note": "also ਸਫ਼ੈਦ (safed); feminine ਚਿੱਟੀ", "r": "chiṭṭā", "t": "ਚਿੱਟਾ"}], "consonants": [{"hint": "oo-rhaa — vowel base, rarely alone", "r": "ūṛā", "t": "ੳ"}, {"hint": "eh-rhaa — vowel base; also the vowel ਅ", "r": "aiṛā", "t": "ਅ"}, {"hint": "ee-rhee — vowel base for ਇ ਈ", "r": "īṛī", "t": "ੲ"}, {"hint": "s as in sun", "r": "sassā", "t": "ਸ"}, {"hint": "h as in hat — also shapes tones", "r": "hāhā", "t": "ਹ"}, {"hint": "k as in kite", "r": "kakkā", "t": "ਕ"}, {"hint": "kh — breathy k, like khaki", "r": "khakkhā", "t": "ਖ"}, {"hint": "g as in go", "r": "gaggā", "t": "ਗ"}, {"hint": "g + low tone in modern speech", "r": "kagghā", "t": "ਘ"}, {"hint": "ng as in sing — almost only in clusters", "r": "ṅaṅṅā", "t": "ਙ"}, {"hint": "ch as in chair", "r": "chachchā", "t": "ਚ"}, {"hint": "chh — breathy ch", "r": "chhahchhā", "t": "ਛ"}, {"hint": "j as in jump", "r": "jajjā", "t": "ਜ"}, {"hint": "j + low tone in modern speech", "r": "jhajjhā", "t": "ਝ"}, {"hint": "ny as in canyon — rare alone", "r": "ñaññā", "t": "ਞ"}, {"hint": "hard T, tongue curled back", "r": "ṭaiṅkā", "t": "ਟ"}, {"hint": "breathy hard T", "r": "ṭhaṭhā", "t": "ਠ"}, {"hint": "hard D, tongue curled back", "r": "ḍaḍā", "t": "ਡ"}, {"hint": "hard D + low tone in modern speech", "r": "ḍhaḍā", "t": "ਢ"}, {"hint": "hard N, tongue curled back", "r": "ṇāṇā", "t": "ਣ"}, {"hint": "soft t, tongue on teeth — like Spanish t", "r": "tattā", "t": "ਤ"}, {"hint": "breathy soft t (never English th)", "r": "thathā", "t": "ਥ"}, {"hint": "soft d, tongue on teeth", "r": "dadā", "t": "ਦ"}, {"hint": "soft d + low tone in modern speech", "r": "dhadhā", "t": "ਧ"}, {"hint": "n as in no", "r": "nannā", "t": "ਨ"}, {"hint": "p as in pin", "r": "pappā", "t": "ਪ"}, {"hint": "ph — breathy p (f in some words)", "r": "phaphā", "t": "ਫ"}, {"hint": "b as in boy", "r": "babbā", "t": "ਬ"}, {"hint": "b + low tone in modern speech", "r": "bhabhā", "t": "ਭ"}, {"hint": "m as in man", "r": "mammā", "t": "ਮ"}, {"hint": "y as in yes", "r": "yayyā", "t": "ਯ"}, {"hint": "rolled r", "r": "rārā", "t": "ਰ"}, {"hint": "l as in love", "r": "lallā", "t": "ਲ"}, {"hint": "between v and w", "r": "vāvā", "t": "ਵ"}, {"hint": "flapped ṛ — like the dd in American 'butter'", "r": "ṛāṛā", "t": "ੜ"}, {"hint": "sh as in shoe (dotted letter)", "r": "sh", "t": "ਸ਼"}, {"hint": "throaty kh as in Khan (dotted)", "r": "kh", "t": "ਖ਼"}, {"hint": "throaty gh as in Ghazi (dotted)", "r": "gh", "t": "ਗ਼"}, {"hint": "z as in zoo (dotted)", "r": "z", "t": "ਜ਼"}, {"hint": "f as in fan (dotted)", "r": "f", "t": "ਫ਼"}, {"hint": "retroflex L — as in ਸੋਲ਼ਾਂ (sixteen)", "r": "ḷ", "t": "ਲ਼"}], "core_nouns": [{"en": "water", "hi": "पानी", "r": "pāṇī", "t": "ਪਾਣੀ"}, {"en": "home", "hi": "घर", "r": "ghar", "t": "ਘਰ"}, {"en": "school", "hi": "स्कूल", "r": "sakūl", "t": "ਸਕੂਲ"}, {"en": "office", "hi": "दफ़्तर", "r": "daftar", "t": "ਦਫ਼ਤਰ"}, {"en": "shop", "hi": "दुकान", "r": "dukān", "t": "ਦੁਕਾਨ"}, {"en": "market", "hi": "बाज़ार", "r": "bāzār", "t": "ਬਾਜ਼ਾਰ"}, {"en": "hospital", "hi": "अस्पताल", "r": "haspatāl", "t": "ਹਸਪਤਾਲ"}, {"en": "station", "hi": "स्टेशन", "r": "station", "t": "ਸਟੇਸ਼ਨ"}, {"en": "airport", "hi": "हवाई अड्डा", "r": "havāī aḍḍā", "t": "ਹਵਾਈ ਅੱਡਾ"}, {"en": "room", "hi": "कमरा", "r": "kamrā", "t": "ਕਮਰਾ"}, {"en": "door", "hi": "दरवाज़ा", "r": "darvāzā", "t": "ਦਰਵਾਜ਼ਾ"}, {"en": "book", "hi": "किताब", "r": "kitāb", "t": "ਕਿਤਾਬ"}, {"en": "phone", "hi": "फ़ोन", "r": "fon", "t": "ਫ਼ੋਨ"}], "counting_note": "Punjabi has no classifiers — put the number straight before the noun. But the noun itself goes plural: ਇੱਕ ਕਿਤਾਬ (one book), ਦੋ ਕਿਤਾਬਾਂ (two books), ਤਿੰਨ ਰੁਪਏ (three rupees).", "culture": [{"en": "The Golden Temple in Amritsar: Sikhism's holiest shrine, open to everyone, day and night.", "r": "Harimandar Sāhib", "t": "ਹਰਿਮੰਦਰ ਸਾਹਿਬ"}, {"en": "The free community kitchen at every gurdwara — sit on the floor, eat dal-roti, all are equal.", "r": "langar", "t": "ਲੰਗਰ"}, {"en": "The spring harvest festival (13 April) — and the Khalsa's birthday. Expect bhangra.", "r": "Vaisākhī", "t": "ਵਿਸਾਖੀ"}, {"en": "The mid-January bonfire festival — peanuts, rewri and folk songs around the fire.", "r": "Lohrī", "t": "ਲੋਹੜੀ"}, {"en": "Punjab's thundering harvest dance — now a global party soundtrack. Women answer with ਗਿੱਧਾ (giddhā).", "r": "bhāngṛā", "t": "ਭੰਗੜਾ"}], "daily_phrases": [{"en": "I wake up at six", "hi": "मैं छह बजे उठता हूँ", "r": "Main chhe vaje uṭhdā hān", "t": "ਮੈਂ ਛੇ ਵਜੇ ਉੱਠਦਾ ਹਾਂ"}, {"en": "I take a bath", "hi": "मैं नहाता हूँ", "r": "Main nahāundā hān", "t": "ਮੈਂ ਨਹਾਉਂਦਾ ਹਾਂ"}, {"en": "I have breakfast", "hi": "मैं नाश्ता करता हूँ", "r": "Main nāshtā kardā hān", "t": "ਮੈਂ ਨਾਸ਼ਤਾ ਕਰਦਾ ਹਾਂ"}, {"en": "I go to work", "hi": "मैं काम पर जाता हूँ", "r": "Main kamm te jāndā hān", "t": "ਮੈਂ ਕੰਮ ਤੇ ਜਾਂਦਾ ਹਾਂ"}, {"en": "I eat lunch", "hi": "मैं दोपहर का खाना खाता हूँ", "r": "Main dupahir dā khāṇā khāndā hān", "t": "ਮੈਂ ਦੁਪਹਿਰ ਦਾ ਖਾਣਾ ਖਾਂਦਾ ਹਾਂ"}, {"en": "I come home in the evening", "hi": "मैं शाम को घर आता हूँ", "r": "Main shām nū ghar āundā hān", "t": "ਮੈਂ ਸ਼ਾਮ ਨੂੰ ਘਰ ਆਉਂਦਾ ਹਾਂ"}, {"en": "I watch TV", "hi": "मैं टीवी देखता हूँ", "r": "Main ṭīvī dekhdā hān", "t": "ਮੈਂ ਟੀਵੀ ਦੇਖਦਾ ਹਾਂ"}, {"en": "I sleep at ten", "hi": "मैं दस बजे सोता हूँ", "r": "Main das vaje saundā hān", "t": "ਮੈਂ ਦਸ ਵਜੇ ਸੌਂਦਾ ਹਾਂ"}], "days": [{"en": "Monday", "hi": "सोमवार", "r": "Somvār", "t": "ਸੋਮਵਾਰ"}, {"en": "Tuesday", "hi": "मंगलवार", "r": "Mangalvār", "t": "ਮੰਗਲਵਾਰ"}, {"en": "Wednesday", "hi": "बुधवार", "r": "Budhvār", "t": "ਬੁੱਧਵਾਰ"}, {"en": "Thursday", "hi": "गुरुवार", "r": "Vīrvār", "t": "ਵੀਰਵਾਰ"}, {"en": "Friday", "hi": "शुक्रवार", "r": "Shukkarvār", "t": "ਸ਼ੁੱਕਰਵਾਰ"}, {"en": "Saturday", "hi": "शनिवार", "r": "Shanivār", "t": "ਸ਼ਨੀਵਾਰ"}, {"en": "Sunday", "hi": "रविवार", "r": "Aitvār", "t": "ਐਤਵਾਰ"}], "dialogues": [{"lines": [{"en": "Greetings! My name is Harpreet.", "hi": "सत श्री अकाल! मेरा नाम हरप्रीत है।", "r": "Sat Srī Akāl! Merā nām Harpreet hai.", "sp": "Harpreet", "t": "ਸਤਿ ਸ੍ਰੀ ਅਕਾਲ! ਮੇਰਾ ਨਾਮ ਹਰਪ੍ਰੀਤ ਹੈ।"}, {"en": "Greetings! I'm Simran. How are you?", "hi": "सत श्री अकाल! मैं सिमरन हूँ। आप कैसे हैं?", "r": "Sat Srī Akāl! Main Simran. Tusīn kiven ho?", "sp": "Simran", "t": "ਸਤਿ ਸ੍ਰੀ ਅਕਾਲ! ਮੈਂ ਸਿਮਰਨ। ਤੁਸੀਂ ਕਿਵੇਂ ਹੋ?"}, {"en": "I'm fine, thanks. Where are you from?", "hi": "मैं ठीक हूँ, शुक्रिया। आप कहाँ से हैं?", "r": "Main ṭhīk hān, shukrīā. Tusīn kitthon ho?", "sp": "Harpreet", "t": "ਮੈਂ ਠੀਕ ਹਾਂ, ਸ਼ੁਕਰੀਆ। ਤੁਸੀਂ ਕਿੱਥੋਂ ਹੋ?"}, {"en": "I'm from Amritsar. Which city is yours?", "hi": "मैं अमृतसर से हूँ। आपका शहर कौन-सा है?", "r": "Main Ammritsar ton hān. Tuhāḍā shahir kihṛā hai?", "sp": "Simran", "t": "ਮੈਂ ਅੰਮ੍ਰਿਤਸਰ ਤੋਂ ਹਾਂ। ਤੁਹਾਡਾ ਸ਼ਹਿਰ ਕਿਹੜਾ ਹੈ?"}, {"en": "I'm from Delhi. I'm learning Punjabi.", "hi": "मैं दिल्ली से हूँ। मैं पंजाबी सीखता हूँ।", "r": "Main Dillī ton hān. Main Panjābī sikkhdā hān.", "sp": "Harpreet", "t": "ਮੈਂ ਦਿੱਲੀ ਤੋਂ ਹਾਂ। ਮੈਂ ਪੰਜਾਬੀ ਸਿੱਖਦਾ ਹਾਂ।"}], "title": "Meeting someone"}, {"lines": [{"en": "Greetings, sir! What will you have?", "hi": "सत श्री अकाल जी! क्या लेंगे?", "r": "Sat Srī Akāl jī! Kī lavoge?", "sp": "Waiter", "t": "ਸਤਿ ਸ੍ਰੀ ਅਕਾਲ ਜੀ! ਕੀ ਲਵੋਗੇ?"}, {"en": "Give us two thalis. Do you have sarson da saag?", "hi": "हमें दो थालियाँ दीजिए। सरसों का साग है?", "r": "Sānū do thālīān dio. Sarson dā sāg hai?", "sp": "You", "t": "ਸਾਨੂੰ ਦੋ ਥਾਲੀਆਂ ਦਿਓ। ਸਰਸੋਂ ਦਾ ਸਾਗ ਹੈ?"}, {"en": "Yes indeed! It tastes wonderful with makki di roti.", "hi": "हाँ जी! मक्की की रोटी के साथ बहुत स्वाद लगेगा।", "r": "Hānjī! Makkī dī rotī nāl bahut savād laggegā.", "sp": "Waiter", "t": "ਹਾਂਜੀ! ਮੱਕੀ ਦੀ ਰੋਟੀ ਨਾਲ ਬਹੁਤ ਸਵਾਦ ਲੱਗੇਗਾ।"}, {"en": "Good — two sweet lassis with that too.", "hi": "अच्छा — साथ में दो मीठी लस्सी भी।", "r": "Changā — nāl do miṭhīān lassīān vī.", "sp": "You", "t": "ਚੰਗਾ — ਨਾਲ ਦੋ ਮਿੱਠੀਆਂ ਲੱਸੀਆਂ ਵੀ।"}, {"en": "Very good, sir! It'll be here in five minutes.", "hi": "बहुत अच्छा जी! पाँच मिनट में आ जाता है।", "r": "Bahut changā jī! Panj minṭ vich ā jāndā hai.", "sp": "Waiter", "t": "ਬਹੁਤ ਚੰਗਾ ਜੀ! ਪੰਜ ਮਿੰਟ ਵਿੱਚ ਆ ਜਾਂਦਾ ਹੈ।"}], "title": "At a dhaba"}, {"lines": [{"en": "Greetings! How much is this shawl?", "hi": "सत श्री अकाल! यह शॉल कितने की है?", "r": "Sat Srī Akāl! Ih shāl kinne dī hai?", "sp": "You", "t": "ਸਤਿ ਸ੍ਰੀ ਅਕਾਲ! ਇਹ ਸ਼ਾਲ ਕਿੰਨੇ ਦੀ ਹੈ?"}, {"en": "Fifteen hundred rupees, sir. Very fine stuff.", "hi": "पंद्रह सौ रुपये की है जी। बहुत बढ़िया चीज़ है।", "r": "Pandrān sau rupae dī hai jī. Bahut vadhīā chīz hai.", "sp": "Shopkeeper", "t": "ਪੰਦਰਾਂ ਸੌ ਰੁਪਏ ਦੀ ਹੈ ਜੀ। ਬਹੁਤ ਵਧੀਆ ਚੀਜ਼ ਹੈ।"}, {"en": "Too expensive! Give it for a thousand.", "hi": "बहुत महँगी है! हज़ार में दीजिए।", "r": "Bahut mahingī hai! Hazār vich dio.", "sp": "You", "t": "ਬਹੁਤ ਮਹਿੰਗੀ ਹੈ! ਹਜ਼ਾਰ ਵਿੱਚ ਦਿਓ।"}, {"en": "No sir, it won't go below twelve hundred.", "hi": "नहीं जी, बारह सौ से कम नहीं होगी।", "r": "Nahīn jī, bārān sau ton ghaṭṭ nahīn hovegī.", "sp": "Shopkeeper", "t": "ਨਹੀਂ ਜੀ, ਬਾਰਾਂ ਸੌ ਤੋਂ ਘੱਟ ਨਹੀਂ ਹੋਵੇਗੀ।"}, {"en": "Fine, pack it for twelve hundred. Thanks!", "hi": "अच्छा, बारह सौ में पैक कर दीजिए। शुक्रिया!", "r": "Changā, bārān sau vich paik kar dio. Shukrīā!", "sp": "You", "t": "ਚੰਗਾ, ਬਾਰਾਂ ਸੌ ਵਿੱਚ ਪੈਕ ਕਰ ਦਿਓ। ਸ਼ੁਕਰੀਆ!"}], "title": "Bargaining at the bazaar"}], "difficulty": "Easy for Hindi speakers — familiar grammar, a new script and gentle tones", "family": [{"en": "mother", "hi": "माँ", "note": "ਮਾਤਾ (mātā) is the formal word", "r": "mān", "t": "ਮਾਂ"}, {"en": "father", "hi": "पिता", "note": "ਪਿਤਾ (pitā) is formal; kids say ਪਾਪਾ too", "r": "pio", "t": "ਪਿਓ"}, {"en": "brother", "hi": "भाई", "note": "elder: ਵੱਡਾ ਭਰਾ; younger: ਛੋਟਾ ਭਰਾ", "r": "bharā", "t": "ਭਰਾ"}, {"en": "sister", "hi": "बहन", "note": "", "r": "bhaiṇ", "t": "ਭੈਣ"}, {"en": "son", "hi": "बेटा", "note": "ਮੁੰਡਾ (muṇḍā) = boy; ਪੁੱਤਰ (puttar) is formal", "r": "putt", "t": "ਪੁੱਤ"}, {"en": "daughter", "hi": "बेटी", "note": "", "r": "dhī", "t": "ਧੀ"}, {"en": "husband", "hi": "पति", "note": "ਘਰਵਾਲਾ (gharvālā) is the homely word", "r": "patī", "t": "ਪਤੀ"}, {"en": "wife", "hi": "पत्नी", "note": "ਘਰਵਾਲੀ (gharvālī) is the homely word", "r": "patnī", "t": "ਪਤਨੀ"}, {"en": "grandfather", "hi": "दादा", "note": "father's father; mother's father is ਨਾਨਾ (nānā)", "r": "dādā", "t": "ਦਾਦਾ"}, {"en": "grandmother", "hi": "दादी", "note": "father's mother; mother's mother is ਨਾਨੀ (nānī)", "r": "dādī", "t": "ਦਾਦੀ"}, {"en": "uncle", "hi": "चाचा", "note": "father's brother; mother's brother is ਮਾਮਾ (māmā)", "r": "chāchā", "t": "ਚਾਚਾ"}, {"en": "aunt", "hi": "मासी", "note": "mother's sister; father's sister is ਭੂਆ (bhuā)", "r": "māsī", "t": "ਮਾਸੀ"}, {"en": "child", "hi": "बच्चा", "note": "", "r": "bachchā", "t": "ਬੱਚਾ"}], "food_phrases": [{"en": "I'm hungry", "hi": "मुझे भूख लगी है", "r": "Mainū bhukkh laggī hai", "t": "ਮੈਨੂੰ ਭੁੱਖ ਲੱਗੀ ਹੈ"}, {"en": "Give (me) water", "hi": "पानी दीजिए", "r": "Pāṇī dio", "t": "ਪਾਣੀ ਦਿਓ"}, {"en": "The bill, please", "hi": "बिल दीजिए", "r": "Bill dio", "t": "ਬਿੱਲ ਦਿਓ"}, {"en": "This is very tasty", "hi": "यह बहुत स्वाद है", "r": "Ih bahut savād hai", "t": "ਇਹ ਬਹੁਤ ਸਵਾਦ ਹੈ"}, {"en": "Give a little more", "hi": "थोड़ा और दीजिए", "r": "Hor thoṛā dio", "t": "ਹੋਰ ਥੋੜ੍ਹਾ ਦਿਓ"}, {"en": "I'm vegetarian", "hi": "मैं शाकाहारी हूँ", "r": "Main shākāhārī hān", "t": "ਮੈਂ ਸ਼ਾਕਾਹਾਰੀ ਹਾਂ"}, {"en": "Go easy on the spice", "hi": "मसाला कम रखिए", "r": "Masālā ghaṭṭ rakkho", "t": "ਮਸਾਲਾ ਘੱਟ ਰੱਖੋ"}], "food_words": [{"en": "flatbread", "hi": "रोटी", "r": "rotī", "t": "ਰੋਟੀ"}, {"en": "naan", "hi": "नान", "r": "nān", "t": "ਨਾਨ"}, {"en": "stuffed flatbread", "hi": "पराँठा", "r": "paronṭhā", "t": "ਪਰੌਂਠਾ"}, {"en": "Amritsari kulcha", "hi": "कुलचा", "r": "kulchā", "t": "ਕੁਲਚਾ"}, {"en": "lentils", "hi": "दाल", "r": "dāl", "t": "ਦਾਲ"}, {"en": "vegetable curry", "hi": "सब्ज़ी", "r": "sabzī", "t": "ਸਬਜ਼ੀ"}, {"en": "rice", "hi": "चावल", "r": "chaul", "t": "ਚੌਲ"}, {"en": "chickpeas", "hi": "छोले", "r": "chhole", "t": "ਛੋਲੇ"}, {"en": "kidney beans", "hi": "राजमा", "r": "rājmān", "t": "ਰਾਜਮਾਂ"}, {"en": "paneer (cheese)", "hi": "पनीर", "r": "panīr", "t": "ਪਨੀਰ"}, {"en": "curd", "hi": "दही", "r": "dahīn", "t": "ਦਹੀਂ"}, {"en": "butter", "hi": "मक्खन", "r": "makkhaṇ", "t": "ਮੱਖਣ"}, {"en": "ghee", "hi": "घी", "r": "ghio", "t": "ਘਿਉ"}, {"en": "lassi (yogurt drink)", "hi": "लस्सी", "r": "lassī", "t": "ਲੱਸੀ"}, {"en": "tea", "hi": "चाय", "r": "chāh", "t": "ਚਾਹ"}, {"en": "samosa", "hi": "समोसा", "r": "samosā", "t": "ਸਮੋਸਾ"}, {"en": "fritters", "hi": "पकौड़े", "r": "pakaūṛe", "t": "ਪਕੌੜੇ"}, {"en": "jalebi", "hi": "जलेबी", "r": "jalebī", "t": "ਜਲੇਬੀ"}], "gender_note": "Every noun is masculine or feminine, and verbs and adjectives agree with it. ਖਾਂਦਾ (khāndā) is a man eating; ਖਾਂਦੀ (khāndī) is a woman eating. ਨੀਲਾ ਘਰ (blue house, m) but ਨੀਲੀ ਕਮੀਜ਼ (blue shirt, f). Citation forms in this course are masculine — the tables always show both.", "gender_title": "Two genders, everywhere", "greetings": [{"en": "Hello! (Sikh greeting)", "hi": "सत श्री अकाल", "note": "'God is truth' — the standard hello, all day, for everyone", "r": "Sat Srī Akāl!", "t": "ਸਤਿ ਸ੍ਰੀ ਅਕਾਲ!"}, {"en": "How are you?", "hi": "आप कैसे हैं?", "note": "ਕੀ ਹਾਲ ਹੈ (kī hāl hai) is the casual 'how's it going'", "r": "Tusīn kiven ho?", "t": "ਤੁਸੀਂ ਕਿਵੇਂ ਹੋ?"}, {"en": "I'm fine", "hi": "मैं ठीक हूँ", "note": "", "r": "Main ṭhīk hān", "t": "ਮੈਂ ਠੀਕ ਹਾਂ"}, {"en": "What is your name?", "hi": "आपका नाम क्या है?", "note": "", "r": "Tuhāḍā nām kī hai?", "t": "ਤੁਹਾਡਾ ਨਾਮ ਕੀ ਹੈ?"}, {"en": "My name is …", "hi": "मेरा नाम … है", "note": "", "r": "Merā nām … hai", "t": "ਮੇਰਾ ਨਾਮ … ਹੈ"}, {"en": "Nice to meet you", "hi": "आपसे मिलकर खुशी हुई", "note": "", "r": "Tuhānū mil ke khushī hoī", "t": "ਤੁਹਾਨੂੰ ਮਿਲ ਕੇ ਖੁਸ਼ੀ ਹੋਈ"}, {"en": "Thank you", "hi": "धन्यवाद", "note": "ਧੰਨਵਾਦ (dhannvād) is the formal/purer word", "r": "Shukrīā", "t": "ਸ਼ੁਕਰੀਆ"}, {"en": "Welcome!", "hi": "स्वागत है!", "note": "literally 'to your honoured arrival'", "r": "Jī āiān nū!", "t": "ਜੀ ਆਇਆਂ ਨੂੰ!"}, {"en": "See you! / Okay then!", "hi": "फिर मिलेंगे!", "note": "the casual goodbye — 'right then!'", "r": "Changā phir!", "t": "ਚੰਗਾ ਫਿਰ!"}, {"en": "Excuse me / Sorry", "hi": "माफ़ करें", "note": "", "r": "Muāf karo", "t": "ਮੁਆਫ਼ ਕਰੋ"}, {"en": "Please", "hi": "कृपया", "note": "", "r": "Meharbānī karke", "t": "ਮੇਹਰਬਾਨੀ ਕਰਕੇ"}, {"en": "Congratulations!", "hi": "बधाई हो!", "note": "", "r": "Vadhāī hove!", "t": "ਵਧਾਈ ਹੋਵੇ!"}, {"en": "yes (respectful); sir/ma'am", "hi": "जी", "note": "the respect particle — ਹਾਂਜੀ yes, ਨਹੀਂ ਜੀ no", "r": "Jī", "t": "ਜੀ"}], "name": "Punjabi", "native": "ਪੰਜਾਬੀ", "negation_note": "ਨਹੀਂ (nahīn) goes before the verb: ਮੈਂ ਨਹੀਂ ਖਾਂਦਾ (I don't eat), ਉਹ ਨਹੀਂ ਆਇਆ (he didn't come). For commands use ਨਾ or ਮਤ: ਇੱਥੇ ਨਾ ਬੈਠੋ (don't sit here).", "negation_title": "Negation with ਨਹੀਂ (nahīn)", "numbers": [{"hi": "एक", "n": 1, "r": "ikk", "t": "ਇੱਕ"}, {"hi": "दो", "n": 2, "r": "do", "t": "ਦੋ"}, {"hi": "तीन", "n": 3, "r": "tinn", "t": "ਤਿੰਨ"}, {"hi": "चार", "n": 4, "r": "chār", "t": "ਚਾਰ"}, {"hi": "पाँच", "n": 5, "r": "panj", "t": "ਪੰਜ"}, {"hi": "छह", "n": 6, "r": "chhe", "t": "ਛੇ"}, {"hi": "सात", "n": 7, "r": "satt", "t": "ਸੱਤ"}, {"hi": "आठ", "n": 8, "r": "aṭṭh", "t": "ਅੱਠ"}, {"hi": "नौ", "n": 9, "r": "naun", "t": "ਨੌਂ"}, {"hi": "दस", "n": 10, "r": "das", "t": "ਦਸ"}, {"hi": "ग्यारह", "n": 11, "r": "giārān", "t": "ਗਿਆਰਾਂ"}, {"hi": "बारह", "n": 12, "r": "bārān", "t": "ਬਾਰਾਂ"}, {"hi": "तेरह", "n": 13, "r": "terān", "t": "ਤੇਰਾਂ"}, {"hi": "चौदह", "n": 14, "r": "chaudān", "t": "ਚੌਦਾਂ"}, {"hi": "पंद्रह", "n": 15, "r": "pandrān", "t": "ਪੰਦਰਾਂ"}, {"hi": "सोलह", "n": 16, "r": "solān", "t": "ਸੋਲ਼ਾਂ"}, {"hi": "सत्रह", "n": 17, "r": "satārān", "t": "ਸਤਾਰਾਂ"}, {"hi": "अठारह", "n": 18, "r": "aṭhārān", "t": "ਅਠਾਰਾਂ"}, {"hi": "उन्नीस", "n": 19, "r": "unnī", "t": "ਉੱਨੀ"}, {"hi": "बीस", "n": 20, "r": "vīh", "t": "ਵੀਹ"}, {"hi": "तीस", "n": 30, "r": "tīh", "t": "ਤੀਹ"}, {"hi": "चालीस", "n": 40, "r": "chālī", "t": "ਚਾਲੀ"}, {"hi": "पचास", "n": 50, "r": "panjāh", "t": "ਪੰਜਾਹ"}, {"hi": "साठ", "n": 60, "r": "saṭṭh", "t": "ਸੱਠ"}, {"hi": "सत्तर", "n": 70, "r": "sattar", "t": "ਸੱਤਰ"}, {"hi": "अस्सी", "n": 80, "r": "assī", "t": "ਅੱਸੀ"}, {"hi": "नब्बे", "n": 90, "r": "nabbe", "t": "ਨੱਬੇ"}, {"hi": "सौ", "n": 100, "r": "sau", "t": "ਸੌ"}], "past_future": [{"en": "I ate (said by a man)", "hi": "मैंने खाया", "r": "Main khādhā", "t": "ਮੈਂ ਖਾਧਾ"}, {"en": "I ate (said by a woman)", "hi": "मैंने खायी", "r": "Main khādhī", "t": "ਮੈਂ ਖਾਧੀ"}, {"en": "I will eat (said by a man)", "hi": "मैं खाऊँगा", "r": "Main khāvāngā", "t": "ਮੈਂ ਖਾਵਾਂਗਾ"}, {"en": "I will eat (said by a woman)", "hi": "मैं खाऊँगी", "r": "Main khāvāngī", "t": "ਮੈਂ ਖਾਵਾਂਗੀ"}, {"en": "I ate bread (verb matches ਰੋਟੀ)", "hi": "मैंने रोटी खायी", "r": "Main rotī khādhī", "t": "ਮੈਂ ਰੋਟੀ ਖਾਧੀ"}, {"en": "We ate", "hi": "हमने खाया", "r": "Asīn khādhā", "t": "ਅਸੀਂ ਖਾਧਾ"}], "postpositions": [{"en": "to", "ex_en": "Give me water.", "ex_r": "Mainū pāṇī dio", "ex_t": "ਮੈਨੂੰ ਪਾਣੀ ਦਿਓ", "hi": "को", "r": "nū", "t": "ਨੂੰ"}, {"en": "from", "ex_en": "I'm from Delhi.", "ex_r": "Main Dillī ton hān", "ex_t": "ਮੈਂ ਦਿੱਲੀ ਤੋਂ ਹਾਂ", "hi": "से", "r": "ton", "t": "ਤੋਂ"}, {"en": "in", "ex_en": "The cat is in the house.", "ex_r": "Billī ghar vich hai", "ex_t": "ਬਿੱਲੀ ਘਰ ਵਿੱਚ ਹੈ", "hi": "में", "r": "vich", "t": "ਵਿੱਚ"}, {"en": "on", "ex_en": "The book is on the table.", "ex_r": "Kitāb mez utte hai", "ex_t": "ਕਿਤਾਬ ਮੇਜ਼ ਉੱਤੇ ਹੈ", "hi": "पर", "r": "utte", "t": "ਉੱਤੇ"}, {"en": "with", "ex_en": "I went with a friend.", "ex_r": "Main dost nāl giā", "ex_t": "ਮੈਂ ਦੋਸਤ ਨਾਲ ਗਿਆ", "hi": "के साथ", "r": "nāl", "t": "ਨਾਲ"}, {"en": "for", "ex_en": "This is for you.", "ex_r": "Ih tuhāḍe laī hai", "ex_t": "ਇਹ ਤੁਹਾਡੇ ਲਈ ਹੈ", "hi": "के लिए", "r": "laī", "t": "ਲਈ"}], "present_note": "The present is stem + -ਦਾ (m) / -ਦੀ (f) + helper: ਹਾਂ (I), ਹੈਂ (tūn), ਹੈ (is), ਹੋ (tusīn — always plural!), ਹਨ (they). So ਮੈਂ ਖਾਂਦਾ ਹਾਂ (I eat, m), ਤੁਸੀਂ ਖਾਂਦੇ ਹੋ (you eat, respectful), ਉਹ ਖਾਂਦੇ ਹਨ (they eat).", "present_table": [{"verb_r": "khāndā hān", "verb_t": "ਖਾਂਦਾ ਹਾਂ", "who_en": "I (male speaker)", "who_t": "ਮੈਂ"}, {"verb_r": "khāndī hān", "verb_t": "ਖਾਂਦੀ ਹਾਂ", "who_en": "I (female speaker)", "who_t": "ਮੈਂ"}, {"verb_r": "khāndā/khāndī hain", "verb_t": "ਖਾਂਦਾ/ਖਾਂਦੀ ਹੈਂ", "who_en": "you (tūn — close friends)", "who_t": "ਤੂੰ"}, {"verb_r": "khānde ho", "verb_t": "ਖਾਂਦੇ ਹੋ", "who_en": "you (tusīn — respectful)", "who_t": "ਤੁਸੀਂ"}, {"verb_r": "khāndā hai", "verb_t": "ਖਾਂਦਾ ਹੈ", "who_en": "he", "who_t": "ਉਹ"}, {"verb_r": "khāndī hai", "verb_t": "ਖਾਂਦੀ ਹੈ", "who_en": "she", "who_t": "ਉਹ"}, {"verb_r": "khānde han", "verb_t": "ਖਾਂਦੇ ਹਨ", "who_en": "they", "who_t": "ਉਹ"}], "pronouns": [{"en": "I", "hi": "मैं", "r": "main", "t": "ਮੈਂ"}, {"en": "you (informal)", "hi": "तू", "r": "tūn", "t": "ਤੂੰ"}, {"en": "you (formal / plural)", "hi": "तुम/आप", "r": "tusīn", "t": "ਤੁਸੀਂ"}, {"en": "this", "hi": "यह", "r": "ih", "t": "ਇਹ"}, {"en": "he / she / that", "hi": "वह", "r": "uh", "t": "ਉਹ"}, {"en": "we", "hi": "हम", "r": "asīn", "t": "ਅਸੀਂ"}, {"en": "they", "hi": "वे", "r": "uh", "t": "ਉਹ"}, {"en": "me / to me", "hi": "मुझे", "r": "mainū", "t": "ਮੈਨੂੰ"}, {"en": "you (informal, to)", "hi": "तुझे", "r": "tainū", "t": "ਤੈਨੂੰ"}, {"en": "you (formal, to)", "hi": "तुम्हें/आपको", "r": "tuhānū", "t": "ਤੁਹਾਨੂੰ"}, {"en": "him / her (to)", "hi": "उसे", "r": "usnū", "t": "ਉਸਨੂੰ"}, {"en": "us / to us", "hi": "हमें", "r": "sānū", "t": "ਸਾਨੂੰ"}, {"en": "my", "hi": "मेरा/मेरी", "r": "merā/merī", "t": "ਮੇਰਾ/ਮੇਰੀ"}, {"en": "your (informal)", "hi": "तेरा/तेरी", "r": "terā/terī", "t": "ਤੇਰਾ/ਤੇਰੀ"}, {"en": "your (formal)", "hi": "तुम्हारा/आपका", "r": "tuhāḍā/tuhāḍī", "t": "ਤੁਹਾਡਾ/ਤੁਹਾਡੀ"}, {"en": "his / her", "hi": "उसका", "r": "usdā/uhdā", "t": "ਉਸਦਾ/ਉਹਦਾ"}, {"en": "our", "hi": "हमारा", "r": "sāḍā/sāḍī", "t": "ਸਾਡਾ/ਸਾਡੀ"}, {"en": "who?", "hi": "कौन?", "r": "kauṇ?", "t": "ਕੌਣ?"}, {"en": "what?", "hi": "क्या?", "r": "kī?", "t": "ਕੀ?"}], "quiz": [{"a": "hello!", "explain": "ਸਤਿ ਸ੍ਰੀ ਅਕਾਲ (Sat Srī Akāl) — 'God is truth' — is the standard Punjabi hello, any time of day.", "id": "pj-01", "lesson": "basics", "level": "beginner", "opts": ["hello!", "goodbye!", "thank you", "sorry"], "q": "What does ਸਤਿ ਸ੍ਰੀ ਅਕਾਲ mean?", "topic": "basics", "type": "meaning"}, {"a": "thank you", "explain": "ਸ਼ੁਕਰੀਆ (shukrīā) is thanks — ਧੰਨਵਾਦ (dhannvād) is the more formal word.", "id": "pj-02", "lesson": "basics", "level": "beginner", "opts": ["thank you", "please", "sorry", "welcome"], "q": "What does ਸ਼ੁਕਰੀਆ mean?", "topic": "basics", "type": "meaning"}, {"a": "ਮੇਰਾ ਨਾਮ … ਹੈ", "explain": "ਤੁਹਾਡਾ ਨਾਮ ਕੀ ਹੈ? = what's your name — answer ਮੇਰਾ ਨਾਮ … ਹੈ (my name is …).", "id": "pj-03", "lesson": "basics", "level": "beginner", "opts": ["ਮੇਰਾ ਨਾਮ … ਹੈ", "ਮੈਨੂੰ ਭੁੱਖ ਲੱਗੀ ਹੈ", "ਚੰਗਾ ਫਿਰ!", "ਛੋਟ ਦਿਓ"], "q": "Someone asks 'ਤੁਹਾਡਾ ਨਾਮ ਕੀ ਹੈ?' — you reply…", "topic": "basics", "type": "usage"}, {"a": "s as in sun", "explain": "ਸ (sassā) is a plain s — ਸ਼ (dotted) is the sh sound.", "id": "pj-04", "lesson": "pronunciation", "level": "beginner", "opts": ["s as in sun", "sh as in shoe", "h as in hat", "k as in kite"], "q": "The letter ਸ sounds like…", "topic": "basics", "type": "vocab"}, {"a": "3", "explain": "ਇੱਕ ਦੋ ਤਿੰਨ — 1, 2, 3.", "id": "pj-05", "lesson": "numbers", "level": "beginner", "opts": ["2", "3", "4", "5"], "q": "ਤਿੰਨ means…", "topic": "numbers", "type": "vocab"}, {"a": "ਦਸ", "explain": "ਦਸ (das) = 10. ਪੰਜ = 5, ਵੀਹ = 20, ਸੌ = 100.", "id": "pj-06", "lesson": "numbers", "level": "beginner", "opts": ["ਦਸ", "ਪੰਜ", "ਵੀਹ", "ਸੌ"], "q": "Which is 'ten'?", "topic": "numbers", "type": "vocab"}, {"a": "20", "explain": "ਵੀਹ (vīh) = 20, ਉੱਨੀ = 19, ਇੱਕੀ = 21.", "id": "pj-07", "lesson": "numbers", "level": "beginner", "opts": ["12", "20", "22", "200"], "q": "ਵੀਹ means…", "topic": "numbers", "type": "meaning"}, {"a": "50 rupees", "explain": "ਪੰਜਾਹ (panjāh) = 50. ਪੰਜ = 5, ਪੰਦਰਾਂ = 15, ਪੰਜ ਸੌ = 500.", "id": "pj-08", "lesson": "numbers", "level": "elementary", "opts": ["5 rupees", "15 rupees", "50 rupees", "500 rupees"], "q": "'ਪੰਜਾਹ ਰੁਪਏ' on a price tag means…", "topic": "numbers", "type": "usage"}, {"a": "a yogurt drink", "explain": "ਲੱਸੀ — sweet or salted — is Punjab's iconic churned yogurt drink.", "id": "pj-09", "lesson": "food", "level": "beginner", "opts": ["a yogurt drink", "a lentil curry", "a flatbread", "a dessert"], "q": "ਲੱਸੀ is…", "topic": "food", "type": "vocab"}, {"a": "this is very tasty", "explain": "ਸਵਾਦ (savād) = taste — say it and any cook will beam.", "id": "pj-10", "lesson": "food", "level": "beginner", "opts": ["this is very tasty", "this is too spicy", "the bill please", "I'm hungry"], "q": "'ਇਹ ਬਹੁਤ ਸਵਾਦ ਹੈ' means…", "topic": "food", "type": "meaning"}, {"a": "ਮੈਨੂੰ ਭੁੱਖ ਲੱਗੀ ਹੈ", "explain": "ਮੈਨੂੰ ਭੁੱਖ ਲੱਗੀ ਹੈ = I'm hungry. ਪਿਆਸ = thirst, ਬਿੱਲ = bill.", "id": "pj-11", "lesson": "food", "level": "elementary", "opts": ["ਮੈਨੂੰ ਭੁੱਖ ਲੱਗੀ ਹੈ", "ਮੈਨੂੰ ਪਿਆਸ ਲੱਗੀ ਹੈ", "ਬਿੱਲ ਦਿਓ", "ਛੋਟ ਦਿਓ"], "q": "You're hungry in Amritsar. You say…", "topic": "food", "type": "usage"}, {"a": "where is the station?", "explain": "ਕਿੱਥੇ (kitthe) = where — the traveller's most useful word.", "id": "pj-12", "lesson": "travel", "level": "beginner", "opts": ["where is the station?", "how much is the fare?", "stop here", "one ticket please"], "q": "'ਸਟੇਸ਼ਨ ਕਿੱਥੇ ਹੈ?' means…", "topic": "travel", "type": "meaning"}, {"a": "ticket", "explain": "ਟਿਕਟ (ṭikaṭ) = ticket; ਕਿਰਾਇਆ = fare; ਸਟੇਸ਼ਨ = station.", "id": "pj-13", "lesson": "travel", "level": "beginner", "opts": ["ticket", "train", "fare", "station"], "q": "ਟਿਕਟ means…", "topic": "travel", "type": "vocab"}, {"a": "ਇੱਥੇ ਰੁਕੋ", "explain": "ਇੱਥੇ ਰੁਕੋ (itthe ruko) = stop here. ਹੌਲੀ ਚੱਲੋ = go slowly.", "id": "pj-14", "lesson": "travel", "level": "elementary", "opts": ["ਇੱਥੇ ਰੁਕੋ", "ਹੌਲੀ ਚੱਲੋ", "ਸਿੱਧਾ ਜਾਓ", "ਟਿਕਟ ਦਿਓ"], "q": "To make the auto stop here, say…", "topic": "travel", "type": "usage"}, {"a": "a man saying 'I eat'", "explain": "ਖਾਂਦਾ (khāndā, -ਦਾ) marks a male speaker; a woman says ਖਾਂਦੀ ਹਾਂ.", "id": "pj-15", "lesson": "grammar", "level": "elementary", "opts": ["a man saying 'I eat'", "a woman saying 'I eat'", "a man saying 'I ate'", "many people saying 'we eat'"], "q": "'ਮੈਂ ਖਾਂਦਾ ਹਾਂ' is spoken by…", "topic": "grammar", "type": "meaning"}, {"a": "ਖਾਂਦੀ", "explain": "ਖਾਂਦਾ/ਖਾਂਦੀ (m/f), ਖਾਂਦੇ (plural/respectful) — adjectives work the same way.", "id": "pj-16", "lesson": "grammar", "level": "elementary", "opts": ["ਖਾਂਦੀ", "ਖਾਂਦੇ", "ਖਾਧਾ", "ਖਾਵਾਂਗਾ"], "q": "The feminine of ਖਾਂਦਾ is…", "topic": "grammar", "type": "vocab"}, {"a": "ਖਾਧਾ", "explain": "ਖਾਧਾ/ਖਾਧੀ (m/f) = ate; ਖਾਵਾਂਗਾ/ਖਾਵਾਂਗੀ = will eat.", "id": "pj-17", "lesson": "grammar", "level": "elementary", "opts": ["ਖਾਧਾ", "ਖਾਧੀ", "ਖਾਵਾਂਗਾ", "ਖਾਂਦਾ"], "q": "The past tense 'ate' (said by a man) is…", "topic": "grammar", "type": "vocab"}, {"a": "it agrees with ਰੋਟੀ (feminine)", "explain": "Punjabi past tenses are ergative: the verb agrees with the object — ਰੋਟੀ is feminine, so ਖਾਧੀ.", "id": "pj-18", "lesson": "grammar", "level": "elementary", "opts": ["it agrees with ਰੋਟੀ (feminine)", "the speaker is female", "it's the future tense", "it's a typo"], "q": "In 'ਮੈਂ ਰੋਟੀ ਖਾਧੀ', why ਖਾਧੀ?", "topic": "grammar", "type": "usage"}, {"a": "see you! (okay then!)", "explain": "ਚੰਗਾ ਫਿਰ (changā phir) — literally 'right then!' — is the casual goodbye.", "id": "pj-19", "lesson": "conversation", "level": "beginner", "opts": ["see you! (okay then!)", "good morning!", "welcome!", "congratulations!"], "q": "'ਚੰਗਾ ਫਿਰ!' means…", "topic": "conversation", "type": "meaning"}, {"a": "welcome!", "explain": "ਜੀ ਆਇਆਂ ਨੂੰ (jī āiān nū) — 'to your honoured arrival' — the warm Punjabi welcome.", "id": "pj-20", "lesson": "conversation", "level": "beginner", "opts": ["welcome!", "sorry!", "good luck!", "bless you!"], "q": "'ਜੀ ਆਇਆਂ ਨੂੰ!' means…", "topic": "conversation", "type": "meaning"}, {"a": "book", "explain": "ਕਿਤਾਬ (kitāb) = book — ਕਲਮ = pen, ਚਿੱਠੀ = letter.", "id": "pj-21", "lesson": "vocabulary", "level": "beginner", "opts": ["book", "pen", "school", "letter"], "q": "ਕਿਤਾਬ means…", "topic": "vocabulary", "type": "vocab"}, {"a": "friend", "explain": "ਦੋਸਤ (dost) = friend — ਦੁਸ਼ਮਣ is the opposite!", "id": "pj-22", "lesson": "vocabulary", "level": "beginner", "opts": ["friend", "brother", "guest", "neighbour"], "q": "ਦੋਸਤ means…", "topic": "vocabulary", "type": "vocab"}, {"a": "asking the price", "explain": "ਇਹ ਕਿੰਨੇ ਦਾ ਹੈ? = how much is this — then counter with ਥੋੜ੍ਹਾ ਸਸਤਾ ਕਰੋ!", "id": "pj-23", "lesson": "shopping", "level": "elementary", "opts": ["asking the price", "ordering food", "asking directions", "saying goodbye"], "q": "'ਇਹ ਕਿੰਨੇ ਦਾ ਹੈ?' is asked when…", "topic": "vocabulary", "type": "usage"}, {"a": "tomorrow — or yesterday!", "explain": "ਕੱਲ੍ਹ (kallh) covers both — tense and context tell you which. ਪਰਸੋਂ = the day beyond.", "id": "pj-24", "lesson": "time-dates", "level": "elementary", "opts": ["only tomorrow", "only yesterday", "tomorrow — or yesterday!", "every day"], "q": "ਕੱਲ੍ਹ means…", "topic": "vocabulary", "type": "meaning"}], "review_deck": [{"en": "hello!", "r": "Sat Srī Akāl", "t": "ਸਤਿ ਸ੍ਰੀ ਅਕਾਲ"}, {"en": "thank you", "r": "shukrīā", "t": "ਸ਼ੁਕਰੀਆ"}, {"en": "yes (respectful)", "r": "hānjī", "t": "ਹਾਂਜੀ"}, {"en": "no; not", "r": "nahīn", "t": "ਨਹੀਂ"}, {"en": "I; me", "r": "main", "t": "ਮੈਂ"}, {"en": "you (formal)", "r": "tusīn", "t": "ਤੁਸੀਂ"}, {"en": "what?", "r": "kī?", "t": "ਕੀ?"}, {"en": "where?", "r": "kitthe?", "t": "ਕਿੱਥੇ?"}, {"en": "how much?", "r": "kinnā?", "t": "ਕਿੰਨਾ?"}, {"en": "who?", "r": "kauṇ?", "t": "ਕੌਣ?"}, {"en": "water", "r": "pāṇī", "t": "ਪਾਣੀ"}, {"en": "bread", "r": "rotī", "t": "ਰੋਟੀ"}, {"en": "home", "r": "ghar", "t": "ਘਰ"}, {"en": "friend", "r": "dost", "t": "ਦੋਸਤ"}, {"en": "day", "r": "din", "t": "ਦਿਨ"}, {"en": "night", "r": "rāt", "t": "ਰਾਤ"}, {"en": "good; okay", "r": "changā", "t": "ਚੰਗਾ"}, {"en": "big", "r": "vaḍḍā", "t": "ਵੱਡਾ"}, {"en": "small", "r": "chhoṭā", "t": "ਛੋਟਾ"}, {"en": "happy", "r": "khush", "t": "ਖੁਸ਼"}], "roman_native": "Panjābī", "script_name": "Gurmukhi", "script_note": "Gurmukhi has 35 core letters — the ਪੈਂਟੀ ਅਖਰ (paintī akhar, 'the 35'). It runs left to right with no headline bar, and its letters look rounder than Devanagari. Six dotted letters (ਸ਼ ਖ਼ ਗ਼ ਜ਼ ਫ਼ ਲ਼) cover Persian sounds, and nasalization is marked with ਬਿੰਦੀ (ਂ) and ਟਿੱਪੀ (ੰ): ਮਾਂ (mān, mother) needs its bindi — drop it and the word breaks. Across the border, Pakistani Punjabi is written in Shahmukhi (Perso-Arabic) — same language, different script. Punjabi is tonal: ਘ ਝ ਢ ਧ ਭ and ਹ colour the pitch of nearby vowels — listen more than you read at first.", "shopping_phrases": [{"en": "How much is this?", "hi": "यह कितने का है?", "r": "Ih kinne dā hai?", "t": "ਇਹ ਕਿੰਨੇ ਦਾ ਹੈ?"}, {"en": "Too expensive!", "hi": "बहुत महँगा है!", "r": "Bahut mahingā hai!", "t": "ਬਹੁਤ ਮਹਿੰਗਾ ਹੈ!"}, {"en": "Make it cheaper", "hi": "थोड़ा सस्ता करिए", "r": "Thoṛā sastā karo", "t": "ਥੋੜ੍ਹਾ ਸਸਤਾ ਕਰੋ"}, {"en": "I'm just looking", "hi": "मैं सिर्फ़ देख रहा हूँ", "r": "Main sirf dekh rihā hān", "t": "ਮੈਂ ਸਿਰਫ਼ ਦੇਖ ਰਿਹਾ ਹਾਂ"}, {"en": "Pack this", "hi": "इसे पैक कर दीजिए", "r": "Ih paik kar dio", "t": "ਇਹ ਪੈਕ ਕਰ ਦਿਓ"}, {"en": "Give a discount", "hi": "छूट दीजिए", "r": "Chhoṭ dio", "t": "ਛੋਟ ਦਿਓ"}], "shopping_words": [{"en": "price", "hi": "क़ीमत", "r": "kīmat", "t": "ਕੀਮਤ"}, {"en": "discount", "hi": "छूट", "r": "chhoṭ", "t": "ਛੋਟ"}, {"en": "cash", "hi": "नक़द", "r": "nakad", "t": "ਨਕਦ"}, {"en": "card", "hi": "कार्ड", "r": "card", "t": "ਕਾਰਡ"}, {"en": "cheap", "hi": "सस्ता", "r": "sastā", "t": "ਸਸਤਾ"}, {"en": "expensive", "hi": "महँगा", "r": "mahingā", "t": "ਮਹਿੰਗਾ"}, {"en": "deal; groceries", "hi": "सौदा", "r": "saudā", "t": "ਸੌਦਾ"}], "slug": "punjabi", "sov": {"en": "I eat bread. (word order: I – bread – eat)", "hi": "मैं रोटी खाता हूँ।", "r": "Main rotī khāndā hān.", "t": "ਮੈਂ ਰੋਟੀ ਖਾਂਦਾ ਹਾਂ।"}, "speakers": "over 120 million", "survival_trio": "ਸਤਿ ਸ੍ਰੀ ਅਕਾਲ! (hello) · ਸ਼ੁਕਰੀਆ (thanks) · ਇਹ ਕਿੰਨੇ ਦਾ ਹੈ? (how much is this?)", "time_words": [{"en": "today", "hi": "आज", "r": "ajj", "t": "ਅੱਜ"}, {"en": "tomorrow; yesterday", "hi": "कल", "r": "kallh", "t": "ਕੱਲ੍ਹ"}, {"en": "day after tomorrow; day before yesterday", "hi": "परसों", "r": "parsōn", "t": "ਪਰਸੋਂ"}, {"en": "now", "hi": "अब", "r": "huṇ", "t": "ਹੁਣ"}, {"en": "morning", "hi": "सुबह", "r": "saver", "t": "ਸਵੇਰ"}, {"en": "afternoon", "hi": "दोपहर", "r": "dupahir", "t": "ਦੁਪਹਿਰ"}, {"en": "evening", "hi": "शाम", "r": "shām", "t": "ਸ਼ਾਮ"}, {"en": "night", "hi": "रात", "r": "rāt", "t": "ਰਾਤ"}, {"en": "hour", "hi": "घंटा", "r": "ghanṭā", "t": "ਘੰਟਾ"}, {"en": "minute", "hi": "मिनट", "r": "minṭ", "t": "ਮਿੰਟ"}, {"en": "week", "hi": "हफ़्ता", "r": "haftā", "t": "ਹਫ਼ਤਾ"}], "travel_phrases": [{"en": "Where is the station?", "hi": "स्टेशन कहाँ है?", "r": "Station kitthe hai?", "t": "ਸਟੇਸ਼ਨ ਕਿੱਥੇ ਹੈ?"}, {"en": "How much is the fare?", "hi": "किराया कितना है?", "r": "Kirāiā kinnā hai?", "t": "ਕਿਰਾਇਆ ਕਿੰਨਾ ਹੈ?"}, {"en": "I want to go to …", "hi": "मुझे … जाना है", "r": "Mainū … jāṇā hai", "t": "ਮੈਨੂੰ … ਜਾਣਾ ਹੈ"}, {"en": "Drive slowly", "hi": "धीरे चलिए", "r": "Haulī challo", "t": "ਹੌਲੀ ਚੱਲੋ"}, {"en": "Stop here", "hi": "यहाँ रुकिए", "r": "Itthe ruko", "t": "ਇੱਥੇ ਰੁਕੋ"}, {"en": "Give me a ticket", "hi": "टिकट दीजिए", "r": "Ṭikaṭ dio", "t": "ਟਿਕਟ ਦਿਓ"}], "travel_words": [{"en": "ticket", "hi": "टिकट", "r": "ṭikaṭ", "t": "ਟਿਕਟ"}, {"en": "train", "hi": "रेलगाड़ी", "r": "rel gaḍḍī", "t": "ਰੇਲ ਗੱਡੀ"}, {"en": "bus", "hi": "बस", "r": "bas", "t": "ਬੱਸ"}, {"en": "aeroplane", "hi": "हवाई जहाज़", "r": "havāī jahāz", "t": "ਹਵਾਈ ਜਹਾਜ਼"}, {"en": "taxi", "hi": "टैक्सी", "r": "ṭaiksī", "t": "ਟੈਕਸੀ"}, {"en": "auto-rickshaw", "hi": "ऑटो", "r": "āṭo", "t": "ਆਟੋ"}, {"en": "station", "hi": "स्टेशन", "r": "station", "t": "ਸਟੇਸ਼ਨ"}, {"en": "bus stand", "hi": "बस अड्डा", "r": "bas aḍḍā", "t": "ਬੱਸ ਅੱਡਾ"}, {"en": "fare", "hi": "किराया", "r": "kirāiā", "t": "ਕਿਰਾਇਆ"}, {"en": "road; way", "hi": "रास्ता", "r": "rastā", "t": "ਰਸਤਾ"}, {"en": "hotel", "hi": "होटल", "r": "hoṭal", "t": "ਹੋਟਲ"}, {"en": "luggage", "hi": "सामान", "r": "sāmān", "t": "ਸਾਮਾਨ"}], "typing": [["ਮਾਂ", "man"], ["ਪਾਣੀ", "pani"], ["ਘਰ", "ghar"], ["ਰੋਟੀ", "roti"], ["ਦਾਲ", "dal"], ["ਚਾਹ", "chah"], ["ਲੱਸੀ", "lassi"], ["ਕਿਤਾਬ", "kitab"], ["ਸਕੂਲ", "school"], ["ਬਾਜ਼ਾਰ", "bazaar"], ["ਦੁਕਾਨ", "dukaan"], ["ਟਿਕਟ", "ticket"], ["ਗੱਡੀ", "gaddi"], ["ਰਸਤਾ", "rasta"], ["ਦਿਨ", "din"], ["ਰਾਤ", "raat"], ["ਸਵੇਰ", "saver"], ["ਸ਼ਾਮ", "shaam"], ["ਮੁੰਡਾ", "munda"], ["ਕੁੜੀ", "kudi"], ["ਦੋਸਤ", "dost"], ["ਪਿਆਰ", "pyaar"], ["ਖੁਸ਼", "khush"], ["ਧੰਨਵਾਦ", "dhannvaad"]], "verbs": [{"ami": "ਮੈਂ ਖਾਂਦਾ ਹਾਂ", "ami_r": "Main khāndā hān", "en": "to eat", "hi": "खाना", "r": "khāṇā", "t": "ਖਾਣਾ"}, {"ami": "ਮੈਂ ਪੀਂਦਾ ਹਾਂ", "ami_r": "Main pīndā hān", "en": "to drink", "hi": "पीना", "r": "pīṇā", "t": "ਪੀਣਾ"}, {"ami": "ਮੈਂ ਜਾਂਦਾ ਹਾਂ", "ami_r": "Main jāndā hān", "en": "to go", "hi": "जाना", "r": "jāṇā", "t": "ਜਾਣਾ"}, {"ami": "ਮੈਂ ਆਉਂਦਾ ਹਾਂ", "ami_r": "Main āundā hān", "en": "to come", "hi": "आना", "r": "āuṇā", "t": "ਆਉਣਾ"}, {"ami": "ਮੈਂ ਕਰਦਾ ਹਾਂ", "ami_r": "Main kardā hān", "en": "to do", "hi": "करना", "r": "karnā", "t": "ਕਰਨਾ"}, {"ami": "ਮੈਂ ਬੋਲਦਾ ਹਾਂ", "ami_r": "Main boldā hān", "en": "to speak", "hi": "बोलना", "r": "bolṇā", "t": "ਬੋਲਣਾ"}, {"ami": "ਮੈਂ ਪੜ੍ਹਦਾ ਹਾਂ", "ami_r": "Main paṛhdā hān", "en": "to read; to study", "hi": "पढ़ना", "r": "paṛhnā", "t": "ਪੜ੍ਹਨਾ"}, {"ami": "ਮੈਂ ਲਿਖਦਾ ਹਾਂ", "ami_r": "Main likhdā hān", "en": "to write", "hi": "लिखना", "r": "likhṇā", "t": "ਲਿਖਣਾ"}, {"ami": "ਮੈਂ ਸਿੱਖਦਾ ਹਾਂ", "ami_r": "Main sikkhdā hān", "en": "to learn", "hi": "सीखना", "r": "sikkhṇā", "t": "ਸਿੱਖਣਾ"}, {"ami": "ਮੈਂ ਦੇਖਦਾ ਹਾਂ", "ami_r": "Main dekhdā hān", "en": "to see; to watch", "hi": "देखना", "r": "dekhnā", "t": "ਦੇਖਣਾ"}, {"ami": "ਮੈਂ ਸੁਣਦਾ ਹਾਂ", "ami_r": "Main suṇdā hān", "en": "to listen; to hear", "hi": "सुनना", "r": "suṇnā", "t": "ਸੁਣਨਾ"}, {"ami": "ਮੈਂ ਲੈਂਦਾ ਹਾਂ", "ami_r": "Main laindā hān", "en": "to take", "hi": "लेना", "r": "laiṇā", "t": "ਲੈਣਾ"}, {"ami": "ਮੈਂ ਦਿੰਦਾ ਹਾਂ", "ami_r": "Main dindā hān", "en": "to give", "hi": "देना", "r": "deṇā", "t": "ਦੇਣਾ"}, {"ami": "ਮੈਂ ਖਰੀਦਦਾ ਹਾਂ", "ami_r": "Main kharīddā hān", "en": "to buy", "hi": "ख़रीदना", "r": "kharīdṇā", "t": "ਖਰੀਦਣਾ"}, {"ami": "ਮੈਂ ਵੇਚਦਾ ਹਾਂ", "ami_r": "Main vechdā hān", "en": "to sell", "hi": "बेचना", "r": "vechṇā", "t": "ਵੇਚਣਾ"}, {"ami": "ਮੈਂ ਸੌਂਦਾ ਹਾਂ", "ami_r": "Main saundā hān", "en": "to sleep", "hi": "सोना", "r": "sauṇā", "t": "ਸੌਣਾ"}, {"ami": "ਮੈਂ ਉੱਠਦਾ ਹਾਂ", "ami_r": "Main uṭhdā hān", "en": "to wake up; to get up", "hi": "उठना", "r": "uṭhṇā", "t": "ਉੱਠਣਾ"}, {"ami": "ਮੈਂ ਬੈਠਦਾ ਹਾਂ", "ami_r": "Main baiṭhdā hān", "en": "to sit", "hi": "बैठना", "r": "baiṭhṇā", "t": "ਬੈਠਣਾ"}], "vowels": [{"hint": "a as in about — the default vowel", "r": "a", "t": "ਅ"}, {"hint": "aa as in father", "r": "ā", "t": "ਆ"}, {"hint": "i as in bit", "r": "i", "t": "ਇ"}, {"hint": "ee as in feet", "r": "ī", "t": "ਈ"}, {"hint": "u as in put", "r": "u", "t": "ਉ"}, {"hint": "oo as in food", "r": "ū", "t": "ਊ"}, {"hint": "ay as in say", "r": "e", "t": "ਏ"}, {"hint": "i as in line", "r": "ai", "t": "ਐ"}, {"hint": "o as in go", "r": "o", "t": "ਓ"}, {"hint": "ou as in loud", "r": "au", "t": "ਔ"}], "where": "Indian Punjab, Pakistani Punjab and a worldwide diaspora"}